HST Office: Segoe UI and Aptos resolve to width-matched bundled fonts when they are not installed.

Neither font has a metric-compatible open replacement, and neither is ever bundled. Both are added to
aMetricCompatibleMap (used on every platform, before the system's own substitution), commented as width
matches rather than metric-compatible ones. Advance widths were measured on English and Vietnamese text; Aptos
from the reference app's own cloud-font cache on the test PC, read in place.

- Segoe UI -> Liberation Sans: 1.003 (English) and 1.014 (Vietnamese) of its width. Noto Sans, the previous
  fallback on Linux, was 1.061 and 1.055.
- Aptos, Aptos Display, Aptos Narrow -> Calibri, which resolves to Carlito where Calibri is missing.
  Carlito is 0.959/0.958 of Aptos (Aptos Display 1.028/1.031, Aptos Narrow 1.044/1.043) with the same line
  height (1.221 em) and x-height (0.478 vs 0.476 em). Liberation Sans is 1.043/1.057 with 8.5 percent lower
  lines; Linux Biolinum G is 0.975/0.982 but has 6.6 percent lower lines and a 9 percent smaller x-height.
- vcl/qa: FindFontFamily(FontSelectPattern&) is exported so the lookup can be unit-tested.

